# Generated, committed cross-agent artifacts (rebuilt by scripts/build-plugins).
# Marking them linguist-generated collapses them in GitHub diffs/language stats and
# exempts them from release-scan's per-commit changed-lines gate (a bulk regeneration
# is not a granularity problem). Source lives under plugins/; never hand-edit outputs/.
outputs/** linguist-generated

# The OKF bundle indexes are GENERATED, and a generated file stored as bytes is a conflict
# generator (2026-09-01, issue #780). `okf/scripts/refresh-index.sh` derives each index from what
# is on disk, so every branch that adds an artifact rewrites the same sorted region — and each
# new artifact reaching the base then conflicts with every open branch that has one of its own.
#
# MEASURED on a consuming repository, 2026-08-31: three open proposal pull requests, every open
# proposal there was, each carrying exactly ONE conflict, and it was `.workaholic/feedbacks/index.md`
# in all three. Nothing about the three asks disagreed. The loop reported the blockage hourly and
# filed two tickets about it while the work behind them sat stranded.
#
# `union` TAKES BOTH SIDES INSTEAD OF CONFLICTING. It is a built-in driver, so it needs no
# per-clone `git config` — which matters here because the sessions that hit this run in fresh
# containers that configure nothing. A conflict in a generated index carries no information: it
# is never a disagreement between two authors, only a stale regeneration, so there is nothing for
# a resolution to weigh.
#
# THE STATED COST: between a union merge and the next `refresh-index.sh`, an index can carry a
# duplicated or mis-sorted line. That is self-healing — the generator rewrites the whole region
# from the tree and runs before every knowledge commit — and it is a strictly better failure than
# a pull request nobody can merge. `conflict-class.sh` keeps its `mechanical` classification for
# the branches that still meet one; this removes the occasion rather than replacing the reader.
.workaholic/*/index.md merge=union
.workaholic/index.md merge=union
